+## Current bounded peer finding — unshown upward gaps
+
+On current generator SHA-256
+`74d53ab4ff66c8067fecd04bbabdeecc99eb1e489723735ac01bd6b7ca49bef4`,
+seed 0/default with sample indices 0,1,2 as demonstrations and index 3 as query
+is underidentified against a simple gap-direction rival. The canonical Racket
+rule and a variant that ignores upward-gap objects produce identical outputs
+for all three demonstrations and different query outputs. Both programs were
+executed through protected Racket (eight executions); the existing
+`lesson_identifiable` hook returns no finding because it checks only the
+4×4-size shortcut.
+
+Reproduce with `workspace/gap_direction_probe.py --out NEW.json` through
+`review.py run`. The full small lesson, exact programs, source/rule binding and
+competing query output are in `counterexamples/gap-direction-teaching.json`
+and the returned `checks/bdcb4c9eb6bd/peer-probe.json`. Preserve this original
+lesson as an optional alternative-answer research example, with reference
+authority and competing interpretation distinguished.
+
+The proposed repair is to select demonstrations covering the gap directions
+needed by queries, or condition query selection on demonstrated directions,
+and add those omission rivals to the teaching check. No production repair or
+approval change was made in this optional peer pass. This new finding does not
+resolve the older validator audit or admit any example to training.
